# Rank 1976 / CVE-2024-31982 (GHSA-2858-8cfx-69m9, CWE-94/95): the
# Main.DatabaseSearch page builds its RSS feed from the raw search text
# (`#set ($text = "$request.text")` feeding `$feed.setTitle`/`setDescription`)
# and then embeds the rendered feed into the wiki page inside the
# `{{{...}}}` escape block (DatabaseSearch.xml:124 at fix parent
# 3c9e4bb04286de94ad24854026a09fa967538e31^):
#
#     {{{$xwiki.feed.getFeedOutput($feed, $xwiki.getXWikiPreference('feed_type', 'rss_2.0'))}}}
#
# The page output goes back through the XWiki rendering transformations, and
# the advisory's PoC closes the escape block from inside the feed title
# (`}}}`) and ships `{{async}}{{groovy}}...{{/groovy}}{{/async}}` in the
# `text` parameter, executing Groovy unauthenticated. The fixed revision computes the
# feed output and writes it straight to the response writer
# (`$response.writer.print($feedOutput)` plus `$xcontext.setFinished(true)`),
# so the value never re-enters the wiki renderer. The weakness shape: a
# velocity reference embedded as wiki content (`{{{$expr}}}`), whose value
# reaches the rendering transformations unescaped for the wiki parser.
#
# Shipped (bindings/config/m2b6375a9.vyql): a `wiki_embed` line event for the
# `{{{$` construct emitted as `code.StoredHtmlWrite` (VYQL-INJ-028, the rule
# that consumes the svelte `{@html`, django `|safe` and erb raw-print
# scopes), beside an `escape` line event for the construct's escaped spelling
# `{{{$escapetool.` credited as `core.HtmlEscape` -- both escape functions are
# documented to escape `{` ("to protect against {{/html}}": XMLUtils.escape
# javadoc, which escapetool.xml wraps, and the escapetool.html override added
# by the sibling library fix). No new concept, rule or rule ID.
#
# Kinship with rank 1975 / CVE-2024-31996 (xwiki-commons escapetool.html):
# this repository owns the call sites, and this ships the wiki-render sink
# half of the pair 1975 prescribed, with the escape control beside it. The
# escape control is only instantiated at the embed spelling, where it
# dominates the sink on the same line; a value-level escape on an ordinary
# print line (the Panels.PanelLayoutUpdate.xml:54
# `$escapetool.html($place)` shape 1975's PoC rides) still cannot be tied to
# the value it wraps, which is the engine gap 1975 filed (config
# text-template escape nodes) -- named here, not re-filed.
#
# Measured on the xwiki-platform checkout at the fixed revision commit:
#   - reachable set of the xwiki_velocity config scope, enumerated by grep:
#     152 xml files carry `<content`, `$request.` and `#`. The `{{{$` embed
#     spelling occurs in 5 of them at the vulnerable revision (4 at the fixed revision); the
#     escaped spelling `{{{$escapetool` occurs 0 times tree-wide.
#   - staged scan of all 152 files: 0 findings before the events, 5 after
#     (3 runs, stable) -- DatabaseSearch.xml:124 (this CVE),
#     XWiki/SearchSuggestSourceSheet.xml:73 and ExtensionSheet.xml:93/95/145,
#     the same construct embedding stored document values. At the fixed revision: 4,
#     the fixed revision's own delta being exactly the DatabaseSearch finding.
#   - the real DatabaseSearch.xml alone: 1 finding at the parent, 0 at the
#     fix. Bounded real-tree scan of the change-carrying search-ui module: 1
#     finding (SearchSuggestSourceSheet), no other rule moved.
# Residuals, stated rather than hidden: an escaped embed silences later
# plain embeds in the same file (the escape dominates every later statement;
# 0 instances tree-wide today), and two embed-carrying files
# (XWikiSyntaxTables.fr.xml, XWiki/UIExtensionSheet.xml) fall outside the
# scope gate because they hold no `$request.` reference. The bare
# `$xwiki.feed.getFeedOutput(...)` print at Main/SolrSearchMacros.xml:936
# embeds request-derived feed content the same way but carries no
# `{{{$` marker; a line-start-anchored match is not expressible in the
# line-contains event kind.
#
# verify_current_expected: fixed.

test "rank1976: feed output embedded as wiki content reports a stored render write"
  lang config
  file DatabaseSearch.xml
  expect VYQL-INJ-028
  code
  ```
  <xwikidoc>
    <web>Main</web>
    <name>DatabaseSearch</name>
    <content><![CDATA[
  #set ($text = "$request.text")
  #set ($feed = $xwiki.feed.getDocumentFeed($list, {}))
  #set ($discard = $feed.setTitle($services.localization.render('search.rss', [$text])))
  #set ($discard = $feed.setDescription($services.localization.render('search.rss', [$text])))
  #set ($discard = $response.setContentType('application/rss+xml'))
  {{{$xwiki.feed.getFeedOutput($feed, $xwiki.getXWikiPreference('feed_type', 'rss_2.0'))}}}
    ]]></content>
  </xwikidoc>
  ```

test "rank1976: writing the feed output straight to the response is clean"
  lang config
  file DatabaseSearchFixed.xml
  reject VYQL-INJ-028
  code
  ```
  <xwikidoc>
    <web>Main</web>
    <name>DatabaseSearch</name>
    <content><![CDATA[
  #set ($text = "$request.text")
  #set ($feed = $xwiki.feed.getDocumentFeed($list, {}))
  #set ($discard = $feed.setTitle($services.localization.render('search.rss', [$text])))
  #set ($discard = $feed.setDescription($services.localization.render('search.rss', [$text])))
  #set ($feedOutput = $xwiki.feed.getFeedOutput($feed, $xwiki.getXWikiPreference('feed_type', 'rss_2.0')))
  #set ($discard = $response.setContentType('application/rss+xml'))
  #set ($characterEncoding = 'utf-8')
  #set ($discard = $response.setCharacterEncoding($characterEncoding))
  #set ($discard = $response.writer.print($feedOutput))
  #set ($discard = $response.setContentLength($feedOutput.getBytes($characterEncoding).size()))
  #set ($discard = $response.flushBuffer())
  #set ($discard = $xcontext.setFinished(true))
    ]]></content>
  </xwikidoc>
  ```

test "rank1976: an embed escaped for the wiki parser is clean"
  lang config
  file SheetEscapedEmbed.xml
  reject VYQL-INJ-028
  code
  ```
  <xwikidoc>
    <web>Main</web>
    <name>Sheet</name>
    <content><![CDATA[
  #set ($text = "$request.text")
  {{{$escapetool.xml($xwiki.feed.getFeedOutput($feed, 'rss_2.0'))}}}
    ]]></content>
  </xwikidoc>
  ```
